---
// The idea, restructured (preview variant). New headline, tighter body,
// and a link out to the full essay at /structure-gap.
---

<section id="idea" class="content-section" aria-labelledby="idea-heading">
  <div class="content-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">The idea</p>
    <h2 id="idea-heading" class="section-headline">The structure gap</h2>
    <div class="section-body">
      <p>
        Agents handle a bounded task well and sustained work badly; the difference is the
        organization around the work — tracking, isolation, independent review, memory,
        escalation — built for humans over decades and never built for agents. Minsky builds
        it into the environment: the same hooks and gates that bind a human bind the agent,
        and they hold without anyone watching.
      </p>
    </div>
    <a class="text-link" href="/structure-gap">Read the full argument →</a>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .content-section {
    padding: 4.5rem 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in oklch, var(--color-text-primary) 4%, transparent);
  }
  .content-inner {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }
  .section-headline {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .section-body p {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 42rem;
  }
  .text-link {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-signal);
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
    transition: color 160ms ease;
    align-self: flex-start;
  }
  .text-link:hover {
    color: var(--color-text-primary);
  }
</style>
